      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "HHT was performed between minimally genetic mismatched inbred strains of rats. There was no evidence of rejection and immunosuppressive therapy was not instituted. Immunohistochemical analysis using peroxidase conjugated monoclonal anti-rat ASMA of cardiac arterioles in which AGAS developed revealed a decreased peroxidase signal. The data suggest that modulation of actin expression in subintimal cells of cardiac arterioles may play a critical role in the pathologic development of AGAS."},
